module_specs:
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top: |
    Integrates the audio_state and pwm_stage RTL blocks with the always-present shell.
    It exposes CLK100MHZ, CPU_RESETN, USB-UART, AUD_PWM, AUD_SD, and the 16-bit LED output.
    The reset asserts asynchronously and releases synchronously into the 100 MHz clock domain.
    The shell owns the USB-UART and decodes the audio_state bus: top registers are placed at
    offsets 0x80, 0x84, and 0x88 in the shell window. AUD_PWM is connected as an open-drain
    output (drive low or release); AUD_SD is held high and LED is held off.
  audio_state: |
    Holds a signed 16-bit sample and unsigned Q15 gain register. Reset clears the sample and
    sets gain to 2068. Shell writes to gain are capped at 8192. sample_out is the signed 16-bit
    floor(sample * gain / 32768) result and is available combinationally. SAMPLE, GAIN, and
    SAMPLE_OUT are exposed through the shell's top register map.
  pwm_stage: |
    Uses a free-running 10-bit counter in the 100 MHz clock domain. Duty resets to 512 and is
    captured from 512 + floor(sample_in / 128) at counter rollover for use in the following
    PWM period. The output is pulled low when counter >= duty and otherwise released to
    high impedance; it is never driven high.

requirements:
  - {id: S-1, text: "The top-level module is c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top and exposes the board-XDC ports for AUD_PWM, AUD_SD, USB-UART, CLK100MHZ, CPU_RESETN, and the 16-bit LED output, plus the CLKS_PER_BIT, TIMEOUT_CYCLES, and BUILD_STAMP parameters.", proof: [analysis, simulation], modules: [c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-2, text: "The sample is a signed 16-bit value that can be written over the shell, is held between writes, and is cleared by CPU_RESETN; sample_out is a combinational signed 16-bit result.", proof: [simulation], modules: [audio_state]}
  - {id: S-3, text: "The gain register is unsigned Q15, resets to 2068, accepts shell writes, and stores 8192 instead of any written value greater than 8192.", proof: [simulation], modules: [audio_state]}
  - {id: S-4, text: "sample_out equals floor(sample multiplied by gain divided by 32768), with the result represented as a signed 16-bit value.", proof: [simulation, analysis], modules: [audio_state]}
  - {id: S-5, text: "A free-running 10-bit counter advances from the 100 MHz clock and repeats every 1024 clocks, giving a nominal 97.7 kHz PWM carrier.", proof: [simulation, analysis], modules: [pwm_stage]}
  - {id: S-6, text: "The PWM duty value is 512 plus floor(sample_out divided by 128), and is updated once per PWM period.", proof: [simulation, analysis], modules: [pwm_stage]}
  - {id: S-7, text: "AUD_PWM is pulled low when the PWM counter is greater than or equal to the duty value and is otherwise high impedance; it is never driven high.", proof: [simulation, hardware], modules: [pwm_stage, c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-8, text: "AUD_SD is always high.", proof: [simulation, hardware], modules: [c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-9, text: "The 16-bit LED output is always off.", proof: [simulation, hardware], modules: [c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-10, text: "The shell communicates over the USB-UART at 115200 baud and supports writing the sample, writing the gain, and reading back sample_out.", proof: [simulation, hardware], modules: [audio_state, c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-11, text: "The design closes timing at 100 MHz.", proof: [analysis, hardware], modules: [audio_state, pwm_stage, c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-12, text: "Simulation verifies reset behavior, gain writes of 65535, 4000, 8192, and 8193, a reset after a write, and sample values including 0, +32767, and -32768 held for several PWM periods; it checks sample_out, low-clock counts measured at AUD_PWM, and AUD_SD.", proof: [simulation], modules: [audio_state, pwm_stage, c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}
  - {id: S-13, text: "The top-level exposes CLKS_PER_BIT, TIMEOUT_CYCLES, and BUILD_STAMP as parameters, and introduces no other time constants.", proof: [analysis], modules: [c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top]}

