module_specs:
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top: |
    Integrates audio_state and pwm_stage with the always-present shell. The shell owns the USB-UART
    pins and register window. The design uses CLK100MHZ and CPU_RESETN, and exposes AUD_PWM,
    AUD_SD, and the 16-bit LED output. Reset asserts asynchronously and releases synchronously
    into the clock domain. AUD_PWM is open-drain style, AUD_SD is held high, and LED is held off.
    The shell protocol is shell/PROTOCOL.md version 1.0.
  audio_state: |
    Holds a signed 16-bit sample and unsigned Q15 gain register. Reset clears the sample and sets
    gain to 2068. Shell writes to gain are capped at 8192. sample_out is the signed 16-bit
    floor(sample * gain / 32768) result and is available combinationally.
    The shell register map uses SAMPLE at offset 0x00 (RW, reset 0), GAIN at offset 0x01
    (WO, reset 0), and SOUT at offset 0x02 (RO, reset 0). Each is 32 bits; bits [15:0] hold
    the sample, written gain, or sample_out, respectively, and bits [31:16] read as zero.
    SAMPLE and SOUT use two's-complement values. GAIN writes set the gain, capped at 8192;
    the GAIN register cannot be read back and reads as zero. Unmapped offsets read zero;
    writes to unmapped offsets and RO registers are ignored.
  pwm_stage: |
    Uses a free-running 10-bit counter in the 100 MHz clock domain. Duty resets to 512 and is
    captured from 512 + floor(sample_in / 128) at counter rollover for use in the following
    PWM period. The output is pulled low when counter >= duty and otherwise released to
    high impedance; it is never driven high.

